How it fits the flow:
- After email/password signup and collecting first/last name, navigate to ProfileDetailsPage.
- User picks a photo (optional) and enters weight/height/body type, then taps Save.
- Photo uploads to Storage at users/<uid>/profile.jpg; Firebase Auth profile is updated with displayName/photoURL; Firestore users/<uid> is written with all fields.
- Navigate to ProfilePage, which streams users/<uid> and displays the saved data.

Below are ProfileDetailsPage and ProfilePage that align with the previously established services (UserRepository, StorageService, AuthService) and complete your onboarding:

- ProfileDetailsPage:
  - Lets the user pick a profile photo (camera/gallery) with image_picker.
  - Validates and collects weight (kg), height (cm), and body type.
  - Uploads the photo via StorageService.
  - Saves weight, height, bodyType, and photoUrl to Firestore users/<uid> via UserRepository.
  - Navigates to ProfilePage on success.

- ProfilePage:
  - Streams the Firestore users/<uid> document using UserRepository and displays the name, email, photo, weight, height, and body type.

